+# HARNESS_LOG — defect 05: dasha predictions show an error
+
+## Investigation
+- Client: `components/dasha/DashaTimeline.tsx` POSTs to `/api/dasha`; any non-2xx shows `data.error`.
+- Route: `app/api/dasha/route.ts` calls `generateDashaPrediction(prompt)` then `prepareJsonString(raw)`.
+  Its comment says "no more assistant prefill is used because newer Claude models reject it".
+- `lib/claude.ts` `generateDashaPrediction` still sends `messages: [user, { role: "assistant", content: "{" }]`
+  and returns `"{" + block.text`. `MODEL_PRIMARY` is `claude-sonnet-5` (lib/constants.ts), which rejects
+  assistant-message prefill with a 400 → the route's catch returns a 500 → "error, nothing loads".
+  "Worked before, stopped recently" matches the model upgrade to Sonnet 5.
+
+## Plan
+1. In `lib/claude.ts` drop the assistant prefill from `generateDashaPrediction`; send only the user
+   message (keep the strict JSON-only system prompt) and return the model's text via `jsonReplyText`
+   (also gives a clear error on max_tokens truncation). `prepareJsonString` in the route already
+   strips fences / extracts the outermost object.
+2. Add a regression test `lib/claude-no-prefill.test.ts` asserting no call in lib/claude.ts ends the
+   messages with an assistant turn, and that generateDashaPrediction returns the model text unchanged
+   (mocked SDK).
+3. Run `npx vitest run` and `npx tsc --noEmit`.
+
+## Log
+### Change 1 — lib/claude.ts generateDashaPrediction
+Removed the `{ role: "assistant", content: "{" }` prefill. It now sends only the user turn and returns
+`jsonReplyText(response, "Dasha prediction")`.
+### Change 2 — added lib/claude-no-prefill.test.ts (source guard + mocked-SDK tests)
+
+$ npx vitest run
+ Test Files  38 passed (38)
+      Tests  283 passed (283)
+(38 = number of *.test.ts files, including the new lib/claude-no-prefill.test.ts)
+
+$ npx tsc --noEmit
+(no output, exit 0)
+
+Not run (approval not granted in this session): the targeted
+`npx vitest run lib/claude-no-prefill.test.ts --reporter=verbose`, and a `git stash` check that the new test
+fails against the old code. No live Anthropic API call was made.
